# API Service Migration

## Service Layer
- Keep existing service classes and methods
- Update base URLs to work with Next.js environment
- Consider using Next.js API routes for backend communication
- Maintain existing error handling patterns

## Hook Migration
- Adapt custom hooks to work with Next.js
- Consider using React Query/TanStack Query for server state
- Keep existing state management patterns
- Update dependencies if needed for Next.js compatibility

## API Configuration
- Use environment variables for API base URLs
- Configure axios interceptors for Next.js
- Handle CORS and authentication properly
- Consider using Next.js built-in fetch for better performance

## Error Handling
- Maintain existing error handling in services
- Use shadcn/ui Toast for notifications
- Implement proper loading states
- Handle network errors gracefully

## Data Fetching
- Consider server-side rendering for static data
- Implement proper loading and error boundaries
- Use React Suspense for code splitting
- Optimize data fetching with Next.js features
